        "original_id": "8489f7f2-25ea-5059-a28b-3533710d3165",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Excuse My French, Pop That\n- People: Machine Gun Kelly, Richard Colson Baker, MGK, French Montana, Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Raekwon, Scarface, Snoop Dogg\n- Places: Cleveland, Ohio\n- Topics: guest appearances, stage names, music career\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Colson Baker was born on April 22, 1990, and is better known by the stage names MGK and Machine Gun Kelly.\n- Machine Gun Kelly is an American rapper and actor from Cleveland, Ohio.\n- Machine Gun Kelly began his musical career as a teenager and released a mixtape in 2006.\n- French Montana's 2013 debut studio album Excuse My French includes guest appearances from Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Machine Gun Kelly, Raekwon, Scarface, and Snoop Dogg, among others.\n- Pop That was released as the first single from French Montana's debut studio album Excuse My French and features Rick Ross, Drake, and Lil Wayne.",
